\0
As the Freedom Guard won its first minor victories and demonstrated that they could challenge the Imperium, popular support for the rebellion spread quickly. Initially, the Freedom Guard armed forces were composed entirely of individuals from the Marked caste. But growing numbers of the common citizenry began to sympathize with the Freedom Guard cause and join in the struggle. Imperium troops attacked civilian populations across the planet Teron, where the first armed resistance had occurred centuries earlier, in an attempt to discourage support for the insurgents.
\1
Imperium forces are butchering civilian populations on Teron. The planet has been a key source of covert resources for the war effort, and we cannot afford to lose our influence in the region. Imperium forces have seized the capitol city of Ankara.  Reclaim Ankara and drive out the Imperium detachment before they can execute the city's inhabitants.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Secure all bridges to control attack routes\n
\s\s\s\s into the city\n
--> Protect the civilian population \n
--> Destroy the Imperium's base in the city
\2
Excellent. You are surpassing my expectations.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Freedom Guard armor engaged the lightly armed Imperium execution squad outside of Ankara and quickly broke the enemy's ranks. The Freedom Guard regiment hunted the disorganized Imperium troops through the city and eliminated the majority of them.\n\n
A mob of armed citizens captured several Imperium Guardians and dragged them to the city courtyard, the same courtyard where an Exploratory Corps crew was executed for mutinying and seizing an Imperium cruiser over 200 years earlier. The crowd tied the Guardians between two Freedom Guard tanks and quartered them.
\3
You appear to be incapable of what is asked of you.
